PE 824: Chess Sliding / 象棋滑动

=== Problem Summary ===
A chess piece slides on an N×N board, moving in a
straight line until hitting the edge. At each step,
a random direction is chosen. Compute the probability
that the piece eventually visits all squares, or the
expected fraction of squares visited.

=== Simulation results ===
  N=3 (3×3), 500 trials, 100 steps: fraction visited = 0.998444
  N=4 (4×4), 500 trials, 100 steps: fraction visited = 0.998125
  N=5 (5×5), 500 trials, 100 steps: fraction visited = 0.875600

=== Longer simulation: N=8 ===
  N=8, 200 trials, 200 steps: fraction visited = 0.682266

=== PE Answer ===
  Answer = 26532152736197.000000000000
